build/*

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# targets/game/reverse/exports.csv, targets/game/reverse/ghidra_functions.csv and targets/game/reverse/string_xrefs.tsv
# are NOT ignored. They are derived from the baseline binary, but so is the
# committed targets/game/reverse/vtables.tsv, and withholding them silently cripples every
# fresh clone: harvest.py opens exports.csv unguarded and dies without it, and
# next_work.py's structural tier drops from 493 candidates to 1 and its Ghidra
# tier reports "outputs unavailable". Regenerating them needs Ghidra plus a
# JDK 21, which no drive-by contributor will do. 2.8MB against the 256MB of
# toolchains and baselines this repo already ships.
# The game-test rig's local configuration: X display numbers DETECTED by
# gpu-displays.sh and absolute wine prefix paths. Machine-specific by
# construction, and committing it would drive whatever holds those numbers on
# the next machine.
.env

targets/game/reverse/.add_match.lock
targets/game/reverse/zh_sweep/locate_state.json

# Alternate-case sweep shims: only the canonical spelling of each dual-case
# include is committed (a case-only-colliding path breaks Windows/macOS checkout).
# tools/gen_case_shims.py regenerates these at build time on case-sensitive FSes.
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/mss.h
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/wsys/file.h
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/stdAfx.h
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/WorldBuilder.h
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/wpaudio/Source.h
inputs/reference/shims/sweep/D3DX8Math.h

# ledger_io.py writes <name>.tmp-<pid> and renames it into place. A process killed
# between the write and the rename leaves one behind; two 23 MB ones were committed
# by a broad `git add` on 2026-09-06 and shipped to every clone.
targets/game/reverse/*.tmp-*
